(Title) Tj
T*
(Rehabilitation Session Characteristics and Activity Levels in Post-Stroke Inpatient Care) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(Abstract) Tj
T*
(We characterized rehabilitation intensity during inpatient physical therapy sessions) Tj
T*
(across Canadian rehabilitation centers. One hundred sixty-six stroke survivors \(mean age) Tj
T*
(69 years, 42% female\) admitted for inpatient rehabilitation were assessed during a single) Tj
T*
(midpoint rehabilitation session using wearable monitors. Mean aerobic exercise time) Tj
T*
(\(defined as >40% of individual heart rate reserve\) was 11 minutes \(SD 12\) per session,) Tj
T*
(with wide variability. Mean step count was 1,030 steps \(SD 620\). Aerobic minutes and step) Tj
T*
(count showed negligible correlation \(R≤ = 0.002\), suggesting these represent relatively) Tj
T*
(independent dimensions of activity. Participants achieving >=20 aerobic minutes during the) Tj
T*
(session \(22% of sample\) were more likely to be male, have lower baseline walking distance,) Tj
T*
(and have subcortical stroke location. No significant demographic differences were observed) Tj
T*
(in mean step count. Current practice falls substantially short of guideline) Tj
T*
(recommendations for aerobic intensity. Session content appeared to emphasize stepping) Tj
T*
(activities over cardiovascular conditioning. These findings highlight a potential) Tj
T*
(implementation gap between recommended stroke rehabilitation protocols and typical) Tj
T*
(clinical practice.) Tj
ET
